{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Za2ndF9aceGQT764isRsD","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, I found the decision regarding the `group.protocol` client configuration in the discussion threads for **KIP-1274: Deprecate and remove support for Classic rebalance protocol in KafkaConsumer**.\\\\n\\\\n## Final Decision\\\\n\\\\n**The `group.protocol` configuration will be removed entirely** (not kept and restricted to a single allowed value).\\\\n\\\\nThis is explicitly stated by Lianet Magrans in her response on February 14, 2026:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"I clarified in the KIP around the group.protocol config. The intention is indeed to deprecate the public-facing group.protocol config in 5.0 and remove in 6.0.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nShe further notes:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"Also updated the content around the group.protocol property, going back to the initial proposal of removing it as unneeded after the transition.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe decision emerged from a concern raised by Matthias J. Sax on February 13, 2026, who questioned whether having only one allowed value (\\\\\\\"consumer\\\\\\\") for `group.protocol` in Kafka 6.0 would be odd, suggesting that removing the config entirely might be better. Lianet's response clarified that this is indeed the approach chosen—the configuration will be deprecated in version 5.0 and removed entirely in version 6.0, rather than being kept with restrictions.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/02/13/mail-b96c0c41bad0fc9745839b89-22fe5f2c.md` (Matthias J. Sax's question)\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/02/14/mail-e437a5f929aa48c75a64ae98-2f7ec638.md` (Lianet Magrans's clarification of the decision)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"README.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/02/28/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21603-opened-6c5c4a55.md\\\",\\\"kips/kip-1191.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/01/15/github-api-apache-kafka-review-comment-PR